 &lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Long mode can add a REX prefix between the legacy prefixes and opcode. VEX, XOP,
and EVEX encodings replace parts of this layout for newer instruction families.
Regardless of the form, an architectural x86 instruction cannot exceed 15 bytes.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>x86 Instruction Families</title><link>https://example.org/x86-instructions/</link><pubDate>Thu, 24 Feb 2022 03:27:04 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/x86-instructions/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;x86 groups a large, irregular instruction set behind common data movement,
arithmetic, bit manipulation, control-flow, and string-processing patterns.
Operand size, address size, execution mode, prefixes, and ISA extensions can
change an instruction&amp;rsquo;s encoding or availability. Intel&amp;rsquo;s and AMD&amp;rsquo;s architecture
manuals remain authoritative; successful assembly only proves that a tool can
encode the source.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="data-movement-and-address-generation"&gt;
 Data Movement and Address Generation
 &lt;a href="#data-movement-and-address-generation" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;MOV&lt;/code&gt; copies an immediate or register value to a register or memory, or copies
memory to a register. An ordinary &lt;code&gt;MOV&lt;/code&gt; has at most one explicit memory operand.
&lt;code&gt;MOVZX&lt;/code&gt; zero-extends a narrower integer, while &lt;code&gt;MOVSX&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;MOVSXD&lt;/code&gt; sign-extend.
A 32-bit general-purpose-register destination in 64-bit mode implicitly clears
the upper 32 bits.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>CPU Architecture Overview</title><link>https://example.org/cpu-overview/</link><pubDate>Thu, 15 Jul 2021 15:11:38 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/cpu-overview/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A processor implements an instruction set architecture (ISA): the contract that
defines instructions, registers, data types, address formation, exceptions, and
privilege behavior. A &lt;strong&gt;microarchitecture&lt;/strong&gt; implements that contract with
pipelines, execution units, caches, predictors, and internal queues. Programs
observe architectural state; performance depends on microarchitectural state.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="from-fetch-to-retirement"&gt;
 From Fetch to Retirement
 &lt;a href="#from-fetch-to-retirement" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;At a conceptual level, a processor fetches instruction bytes, decodes an
instruction, obtains operands, executes the operation, accesses memory when
required, and commits the result. A simple processor can perform those steps
sequentially. A pipelined processor overlaps steps from several instructions,
thus improving throughput without requiring every instruction to have low
latency.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>